{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan","id":979475,"title":"Seriously is every friggin Solar an Orphan?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-30T21:17:08-07:00","id":979475,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon4.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Seriously is every friggin Solar an Orphan?","content":"Okay in my games, with Exalted Especially, players always want to make Oprhans. Yeah I get RPGs are escapism and allows people to avoid all the baggage of Family that they have in the real world, but in my current Game everyone is an Orphan, well almost, one player last minute changed his character from family lost to a bandit attack, to nah he left in his teens.<br /> <br /> And even more rare I never have anyone play someone who is married, but I guess that is probably because I've had experience playing games as a young person and also playing with fellow youths.<br /> <br /> But I've done things like incentivize people towards the vulnerability of family and friends by giving them bonuses like EXP at character creation. Because that seems to be the only damn way to get a group of non-hobo orphans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:27:51-07:00","id":979483,"title":"","content":"But doesn't everyone truly aspire to be part of a roaming pack of murder-hobos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:35:15-07:00","id":979486,"title":"","content":"I don't really have a problem with this in Exalted, my players are a varied lot. I can think of only one who regularly wants to play an orphan and is only an orphan because he regularly kills his own Father who usually murdered his Mother...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:42:04-07:00","id":979491,"title":"","content":"RPGs can be very Freudian...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:44:15-07:00","id":979493,"title":"","content":"One of the PCs in my game just got married to a Dragon-Blooded, and her family doesn't know he's a Solar Exalt. Yikes!<br /> <br /> One of the characters has dead parents, but the other two have relationships with their family. For my character, her relationship is strained, but she is eager to please them because a part of her is still desperate for approval. Her father is a manipulative merchant prince, and so has been convincing her to do stuff for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:45:22-07:00","id":979494,"title":"","content":"Bad ST experience? Family is always an easy target, since you can't hurt a solar directly easily, especially in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:34:46-07:00","id":979514,"title":"","content":"After a particularly bad spat of one dimensional PCs, I instituted a character creation rule: No Orphans, No Amnesiacs.<br /> <br /> I can't say I enforced it too rigorously, but it made the players at least think about where their characters came from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11476-tk421","name":"TK421","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:45:24-07:00","id":979517,"title":"","content":"Man. My group's poor Realmies probably WISH they were orphans. The Twilight's family obligations are a centerpiece of the plot, which focuses on the inter-House struggle for the ownership of a relatively wealthy Northern state that's within three months march of the Bull's warpath. I've got two actual orphans who are on opposite ends of the mood spectrum here. One is a typical wandering kung fu hobo, but the other was raised by a crime syndicate that shattered in a night of terror and fire. His Contacts rating is his scattered &quot;siblings&quot;, and they've come up two or three times into the story so far (11 sessions in). Most recently, one of them upped the stakes in a city the Circle &quot;liberated&quot; simply by being present and extremely pregnant. It gave him extra motivation to keep their little coup as bloodless as possible.<br /> <br /> With the exception of the kung fu hobo, all of my players have been drowning me in NPC attachments. It's honestly impossible to include them all. The same would be true even if they were all orphans, so I don't think the lack of parents is intrinsically problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:49:21-07:00","id":979520,"title":"","content":"PCs in my seafaring game:<br /> <br /> Barbus: Both parents alive.<br /> Seamstress: Both parents dead (but one of them is the Silver Prince, who has been dead since before Seamstress was conceived, and it hasn't exactly slowed him down).<br /> Misu: Both parents dead, but his grandmother and great-grandfather are still present in his life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:58:06-07:00","id":979522,"title":"","content":"Hm. This might be a good place to ask this question. I've been playing around with a backstory, but it might be a bit much. Do you, distressed STs, think this backstory too hokey? I imagine a Dawn as the son or daughter of a religiously devout Southern mercenary. Before her (let's go with daughter) birth, it was prophesied that she would be the death of both of her parents. Her mother died in childbirth, and her father raised her to be a warrior because he refused to die a straw death of any sort and swore that he would die in battle. Now that she's Exalted, there is no doubt that she is a worthy foe, and he openly antagonizes her in hope of greeting death properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T23:01:36-07:00","id":979523,"title":"","content":"Current PCs:<br /> <br /> The Twilight: Mother was killed when he was a kid, but then he cared for his father for another <i>thirty years </i>until old age claimed him. Then the character Exalted in his forties. So, not really an orphan?<br /> The Dawn: Only child, but part of a large and prominent extended family in her home city. Also the ghost of her great-great-great(x14) grandfather is her mentor. Family connections are non-optional.<br /> The Eclipse: Stolen from her Varangian birth-parents as a child and raised on an atoll in the west alongside about one hundred other adopted &quot;siblings&quot; some of whom she is still caring for. So I guess &quot;it's complicated&quot;.<br /> The Lunar: Parents are dead, but he still has living <i>children</i> if he can find out where they went.<br /> <br /> So, not really a problem here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T23:47:14-07:00","id":979531,"title":"","content":"I think one PC in my game had parents who died when she was in her 20s (as they were the King and Queen, this is important because it led to her power struggle for the Realm). And another has dead parents because he was trapped in the Wyld for hundreds of years.<br /> But I don't think that really counts.<br /> <br /> In all the games I play/run at the moment, I think there's only one orphan, as his character was &quot;street kid&quot;, but now he has two adoptive fathers.<br /> <br /> So, I think Eldagusto's experience is a bit strange. My guess is people just don't want their parents intruding on their character's plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T00:03:42-07:00","id":979536,"title":"","content":"The more I think about the original post, the more of an <i>opportunity</i> it seems to be. Your players only think that their characters' parents are dead, after all. You should have a NPC make some honest inquiry as to the PCs family history. As each of them tells the story of how they were orphaned, take careful notes. If you have an Obvious Bad Guy, drop oversized hints about how much he or she resembles one of the PCs. Throw references to the events they mention into every description of every scene, item, character that you can manage. Get your players convinced that not only is the Big Bad one of their fathers or mothers, but that EVERY LAST ONE of their parents is secretly alive somehow.<br /> <br /> Of course, none of them are. They're orphans. But allude to the possibility until they strangle you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T01:19:23-07:00","id":979551,"title":"","content":"Hm, my main Solars...<br /> <br /> Dawn - Her mortal parent is dead, but she's on VERY good terms with her Elemental mother.<br /> <br /> Twilight - His father died in a war for Lookshy over a decade prior to the start of the game, but his mother is alive and well. GM recently hit me with a development that at one point, she and several friends were looking into exposing corruption in the General Staff, but THAT movement was taken out when one of their members was found guilty of a dishonorable murder and exiled.<br /> <br /> Eclipse - Both of her parents are perfectly fine. They're almost criminally dull. Dad's a fisherman, mom's a fisher's wife. She's actually really embarrassed by such modest background, so if asked what her family does she invents different stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T02:11:29-07:00","id":979558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After a particularly bad spat of one dimensional PCs, I instituted a character creation rule: No Orphans, No Amnesiacs.<br /> <br /> I can't say I enforced it too rigorously, but it made the players at least think about where their characters came from. </div> </div> </div>Our Vampire LARP had the &quot;no amnesiacs&quot; rule too.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T02:33:08-07:00","id":979559,"title":"","content":"My favorite character I've made was Mnemon's daughter. So not an orphan.<br /> <br /> Then again, my second favorite was Desus's son....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T02:47:53-07:00","id":979561,"title":"","content":"My Solar ran away from her Lookshy noble family to become a Yozi cultist, then later sacrificed her memories of them as her initiation into terrestrial sorcery.<br /> Funnily enough, her family DID pop up again, and she's managed to piece together a few memories of them. It was a VERY awkward reunion, with a lot of face punching involved.<br /> <br /> The other members of the Circle don't seem to have living family that they know of. One of them is even a self-made orphan. A lack of parentage DOES seem to be a common Exalt trait though. Probably explains why so many of them run off to become murderhobos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, listen to our tabletop podcast! <a href=\"https://sponsoredbynobody.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://sponsoredbynobody.podbean.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11150-king_iniquitous","name":"King_Iniquitous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T03:11:44-07:00","id":979567,"title":"","content":"I think it's more that it's the common trait of hero-protagonists. Look at how many superheroes are orphans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T05:54:27-07:00","id":979614,"title":"","content":"Plenty of times family isn't really mentioned in PC backstories since it doesn't really matter or the player isn't really interested in it, and that's fine. As for my own Solars over the years I've had:<br /> <br /> -Ex-slave. Parents never really mentioned, but a big part of the game was getting back to her far-Eastern tribe.<br /> -Con-artist. Parents still alive, but I don't remember them being an important part of the game.<br /> -Army medic. Parents never mentioned. Probably still alive. He was married with three children, however, so family was important.<br /> -Assassin. Father had died from a battle wound, mother killed in a retaliatory raid. So here we go, an orphan. She was raised by her grandparents, however, who are still alive, along with her elder brother. She's got plenty of family.<br /> -Daughter of a storm ,other. Considering the whole character concept revolves around it, her mother, at least, is still active. Her father was murdered by her mother.<br /> -Blind investigator. Family was killed before game starts, but it happened while they had already been married, had children, in their thirties. Not a child when it happened, so not technically an orphan I guess.<br /> <br /> So I've had only one orphan, and a mix of family importance otherwise. It really depends on the group, the player, and that player's experience, IME.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:00:01-07:00","id":979616,"title":"","content":"I inherited my current group of players from a really awful GM, and it took <i>years</i> for them to move past all the things they started doing in response to things the really awful GM would do - most relevantly to this thread, that would be having literally any friend or family that your character was stated as having be immediately and intensely used as a weapon against your character.<br /> <br /> Character has a sister they like to visit on the holidays? First story arc is that she's been kidnapped and is suffering terrible abuses because someone is mad at your character.<br /> Character has parents they regularly speak with? Their house is on fire, they are inside, what do?<br /> <br /> So the players spent a lot of time playing characters that either didn't have anything/anyone they cared about just trying to get any kind of action besides &quot;save your background details from utter annihilation!&quot;<br /> <br /> In my experience, all it took was time spent seeing that I wasn't going to do the same things as their really awful GM would do, and the players started wanting to have all those details and connections for their characters so that we could have some of the other kinds of stories that involve family and friends, like pleasant down-time between difficult events of the chronicle, or even mild troubles which they could be helped out of like &quot;I need a new roof but I don't have the money to hire roofers&quot; instead of ransom demands on threat of death.<br /> <br /> And all that said, if my group ended up coming to the table with a squad of orphans - fate seems like the kind of thing that would draw orphans together into a tight-knit family-like unit, so lets tell that kind of story this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:23:03-07:00","id":979620,"title":"","content":"I think my tolerance for cliches is much higher when playing vanilla Exalted with Solars.<br /> I'm already writing off things like &quot;how the fuck did we all find each other?&quot; so if I've got no serious plans for my character's parents they're probably long dead or were forced to give her over to someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:43:55-07:00","id":979625,"title":"","content":"Well, one of my favorite characters is a Dawn caste that's an orphan in both directions, if you can call it that. Parents died of natural causes(namely, being tribal beastmen in the far East), and her two children were taken by a raid from another tribe and given to the Fair Folk to never be seen again. After killing every man, woman, and child in the tribe that raided hers(she, uh, kinda hit limit break there), she just left her homeland entirely, has no intentions of ever going back, and has no real goals beyond finding a good fight.<br /> <br /> OOC plans I've though of is that I'd like for her to head up something like a very widespread system of orphanages, given her sorrow over her lost children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:02:05-07:00","id":979634,"title":"","content":"If, as the Storyteller, you treat having family and friends as a vulnerability, it is <i>perfectly rational</i> for players to decide to dodge the cheap drama by playing orphans. Real drama comes from dealing with things the players' characters are actually interested in, not pushing them into Yet Another Aunt May story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:18:49-07:00","id":979640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=979634#post979634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aunt May</div> </div> </div> </div>People in the ancient world live <i>that</i> long ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:30:30-07:00","id":979646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ketrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=979536#post979536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I think about the original post, the more of an <i>opportunity</i> it seems to be. Your players only think that their characters' parents are dead, after all. You should have a NPC make some honest inquiry as to the PCs family history. As each of them tells the story of how they were orphaned, take careful notes. If you have an Obvious Bad Guy, drop oversized hints about how much he or she resembles one of the PCs. Throw references to the events they mention into every description of every scene, item, character that you can manage. Get your players convinced that not only is the Big Bad one of their fathers or mothers, but that EVERY LAST ONE of their parents is secretly alive somehow.<br /> <br /> Of course, none of them are. They're orphans. But allude to the possibility until they strangle you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's kind of what I do, though not every single dead person is alive. That is why I find prologues important, a lot of the random NPCs and such in the backstories are going to be brought back throughout the game. A lot people got set on fire too... that's a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:52:31-07:00","id":979656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=979640#post979640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People in the ancient world live <i>that</i> long ?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you made it out of childhood, life expectancy was generally pretty close to the modern standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:12:31-07:00","id":979667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=979656#post979656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you made it out of childhood, life expectancy was generally pretty close to the modern standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, not even close, then? XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:17:20-07:00","id":979671,"title":"","content":"Long story short, OP, no, not every Solar Exalt is an orphan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:25:04-07:00","id":979714,"title":"","content":"Cool story bro.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure it was a rhetorical question for a thread title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:38:09-07:00","id":979726,"title":"","content":"Just because it's a rhetorical question doesn't mean someone won't try and answer it anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:43:07-07:00","id":979730,"title":"","content":"Glad they are!<br /> <br /> I'm finding the data useful. If I get another player I think I will make a point of trying to help them have a family. I find family characters work as touchstones for the whole circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T10:27:02-07:00","id":979746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=979567#post979567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's more that it's the common trait of hero-protagonists. Look at how many superheroes are orphans.</div> </div> </div> </div>It even makes narrative sense. People with families are much less likely to go out and risk all. Parents tend to worry about ensuring their childrens survival first and once the children grow up, vice versa. Orphans don't carry that weight of worry and responsibility.<br /> <br /> In my experience, if players come to the table as Orphans consistently, they are either newbies who already have their hands full with their own character (especially in a crunch heavy system like exalted) or it's their experience that NPC attachments are ticking timebombs. A group made of orphans usually says more about the GM than the players.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10990-beaumis","name":"Beaumis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T10:54:02-07:00","id":979755,"title":"","content":"From my experience none of the players have ever not chosen to be orphans or without family because they are afraid they will be used against them. As most of the people I know are rookies at the games. Often the Prologue is the place for the tragedies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:28:36-07:00","id":979795,"title":"","content":"In the Last Exalted game I played in:<br /> <br /> Night Caste: I think he grew up on the streets, so I think he was an orphan. Anyways his family wasn't important to his character<br /> Dusk Caste: Nothing about the character's parents. He did have a wife and kid, he pretended not to give a fuck about, so his deathlord would leave them alone.<br /> Twilight Caste: Huge Lookshy Military family. Oldest Brother was an Dragonblooded Ally.<br /> <br /> Personally, my characters do have family somewhere. If they were an orphan, they have people who they consider family.<br /> <br /> As a GM, I like when my players have people they care about (family by blood or family by choice). What makes a better story, the Fae kidnapping random dude number three or your brother? I like my players to be emotionally invested in the story. Yet I try not to distress them so much that they will never make an emotionally vulnerable character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 10-01-2016, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:46:07-07:00","id":979830,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem may just be that with all the stuff going on with villains, allies, other PCs, there isn't a huge amount of room for family in the story, and it's often like that in fiction as well, especially when the story contains an ensemble of heroes instead of getting to focus on the ties of just one person.<br /> <br /> Exalted especially, since most of the time relatively average people are the immediate family of a demi-god, Also because often times exalts range far afield of their home. Ma and Pa Kent don't usually get super involved with stuff in the Justice League plotlines, basically. I wouldn't necessarily pin it on player paranoia or lack of investment/imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:58:24-07:00","id":979835,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's fair. Some PCs just have ordinary parents who live in their hometowns and don't interact with the adventure much.<br /> It's still nice for them to be there for the PC to go and talk to. Like how Superman sometimes visits the Kents for some old-timey farmboy wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:11:27-07:00","id":979843,"title":"","content":"I had a Dawn who started out single, a town guardsman, who dropped by his brothers' for home cooking and to play with the nephews. When a fire broke out in the brothers house, he rushed over to see a nephew and his sister-in-law clinging to his brother, so Brother would not go back into the blaze for the other boy. He burst through a fire weakened wall and rescued the other boy, Exalting to do it. So, no mention or even thought of parents at the time, but family just the same.<br /> <br /> Another Solar, an Eclipse, was a young bureaucrat, and his wealth/resources was explained by deceased parents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like my Avatar? Courtesy of<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Jen</span>! : <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anybody want their characters to be experimented on ? </span>post 98<br /> <i>An Exalt is never unarmed.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4018-l-het-esh","name":"L'het'esh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:15:18-07:00","id":979908,"title":"","content":"Having parents in a tabletop RPG is specifically an invitation for the GM to make use of those parents at some point, in much the same way you might have a backstory hook like a lost throne or a stolen sword or a crimeboss nemesis. The fact that in reality most people have parents but not everyone has a crimeboss nemesis doesn't stop them from being <i>narratively</i> equivalent. Thus, you're going to have a lot of orphans just because that's the default state of PCs.<br /> <br /> (Now, you can always tweak the formula's nose, like my Infernal, who was an orphan but had both a biological sister, who was a Solar, and foster parents, who never really came up.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:18:58-07:00","id":979914,"title":"","content":"I get the impression people here seem to often view family in Danger in an Exalted game as a bug rather then a feature... which is puzzling...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:31:43-07:00","id":979925,"title":"","content":"Lemme crosscheck my party.<br /> <br /> Dawn: Orphan, engaged to a friend of the party, lots of family drama with half-siblings and whatnot<br /> Eclipse: Orphan, on-and-off boyfriend, older sister<br /> Night: Orphan, married, has a child (they're a Gethin - adopted, long story)<br /> Twilight: Deceased mother, father's still alive, on good terms with her sister<br /> Zenith: Estranged parents, no family stuff<br /> <br /> The amount of orphans in my party really doesn't make a difference to me, seeing as they all arrived at that conclusion in meaningful ways and the loss of one or more parents actually affected them and how they see the world. Nobody is an orphan purely for plot convenience.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:56:48-07:00","id":979936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=979914#post979914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the impression people here seem to often view family in Danger in an Exalted game as a bug rather then a feature... which is puzzling...</div> </div> </div> </div>Bad guys shoving your mom in a freezer gets old after the thirty-seventh time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T18:28:15-07:00","id":979981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=979936#post979936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bad guys shoving your mom in a freezer gets old after the thirty-seventh time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to say blase to the point of passe, but that's a good way of putting it. Exalted should be EPIC, not old hat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like my Avatar? Courtesy of<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Jen</span>! : <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anybody want their characters to be experimented on ? </span>post 98<br /> <i>An Exalt is never unarmed.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4018-l-het-esh","name":"L'het'esh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T18:47:51-07:00","id":979989,"title":"","content":"Ummm yeah that's a given, I sincerely doubt someone is going to kidnap your mortal parents 37 times... this is what we call a strawman gentlemen...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:07:39-07:00","id":979998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=979989#post979989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ummm yeah that's a given, I sincerely doubt someone is going to kidnap your mortal parents 37 times... this is what we call a strawman gentlemen...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they mean seeing it happen across a (large) number of characters, it becomes cliche and old. So, some players make sure it can't happen again by being an orphan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:12:21-07:00","id":980000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=979998#post979998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they mean seeing it happen across a (large) number of characters, it becomes cliche and old. So, some players make sure it can't happen again by being an orphan.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Exalted is about human hearts Creation is dangerous, its lame to not have any family or friends ever, having them gives you something to protect and it goes both ways, they could flourish just as easily as suffer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:13:01-07:00","id":980002,"title":"","content":"Contrasting this, my &quot;signature&quot; Solar character that I like to play most often was a patrician before exalting. I wrote up a grandmother, mother, father, three sisters, one living brother, one deceased brother, and encouraged the Storyteller to add any amount of cousins, uncles, and whatever else. Good ol' Realm life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/994-heroicantagonist","name":"heroicantagonist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar994_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:18:39-07:00","id":980003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980000#post980000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Exalted is about human hearts Creation is dangerous, its lame to not have any family or friends ever, having them gives you something to protect and it goes both ways, they could flourish just as easily as suffer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not talking about just Exalted, I'm talking about tabletop games in general. It's depressingly common for a character that has a family to have said family kidnapped/killed/turned by the GM as a way to motivate a character to follow the GM's plot. And it's gotten to the point that many simply won't have a family to avoid that.<br /> <br /> I mean, that character I mentioned doesn't have a family, but not because of that reason. She doesn't have one because I want her to make one. Another character I have has a lot of family, being from House Iselsi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:37:40-07:00","id":980012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heroicantagonist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980002#post980002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contrasting this, my &quot;signature&quot; Solar character that I like to play most often was a patrician before exalting. I wrote up a grandmother, mother, father, three sisters, one living brother, one deceased brother, and encouraged the Storyteller to add any amount of cousins, uncles, and whatever else. Good ol' Realm life.</div> </div> </div> </div>See that's cool, no one ever detailed that much for me. When people don't even detail the immediate family I am confused, will they be upset when I fill in the detail? Some yes, some no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:41:38-07:00","id":980016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980000#post980000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Exalted is about human hearts Creation is dangerous, its lame to not have any family or friends ever, having them gives you something to protect and it goes both ways, they could flourish just as easily as suffer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being an orphan doesn't preclude having friends. In fact, threatening friends is generally a much better motivator than <i>sigh</i>, your mom is in danger again, because if you've made friends with NPCs you've actually put the time in to get to know them a bit. (Note, this goes out the window if the GM actually lets you spend time with your character's mom!)<br /> <br /> Having parents is a premade &quot;I am attached to this NPC&quot; tag, but if the GM doesn't take the time to give it any emotional weight, it's just tiresome!<br /> <br /> It's sort of like threatening Earth in a sci-fi game. Video games especially. It's like yes, I know I'm <i>supposed</i> to care whether or not the Earth is destroyed, but maybe actually let me visit and spend time on Earth one of these days instead of just saving it all the time? (No, running away from it as fast as my legs will carry me does not count!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:55:33-07:00","id":980117,"title":"","content":"One of the things I'm looking forward to with my pirate character is all the intrigue and conflict of being part of the Lintha Family. I hope part of the drama can come from various interactions with distant relatives and their lackeys rather than always being due to opposition from outsiders. (Of course, it's likely my character will be caught in the middle since the Lintha are traditionally presented as antagonists for PCs.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T23:21:42-07:00","id":980127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=979914#post979914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the impression people here seem to often view family in Danger in an Exalted game as a bug rather then a feature... which is puzzling...</div> </div> </div> </div>Families are great in real life. In RPGs they mostly get in the way of adventuring.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T23:39:13-07:00","id":980133,"title":"","content":"To be fair to Exalted, after you become a Solar, the world girdling religion says that you're an evil possessing demon that needs to be shot on sight. This ....encourages Solars to take up a nomadic lifestyle sooner or later. Such that, even if you're not <i>actually </i>an orphan, you're usually <i>effectively</i> an orphan because your home and family is over 100 miles away.<br /> <br /> To ensure that isn't what happens, the ST kinds needs to set up the game that way. Like, running an urban game and asking everyone to be a native of the city or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T00:10:04-07:00","id":980140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980133#post980133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair to Exalted, after you become a Solar, the world girdling religion says that you're an evil possessing demon that needs to be shot on sight. This ....encourages Solars to take up a nomadic lifestyle sooner or later. Such that, even if you're not <i>actually </i>an orphan, you're usually <i>effectively</i> an orphan because your home and family is over 100 miles away.<br /> <br /> To ensure that isn't what happens, the ST kinds needs to set up the game that way. Like, running an urban game and asking everyone to be a native of the city or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as much of an assumption in 3rd because for one the West is essentially the Wild West and away from both the Guild and established Realm holdings, the East is buffered by the Scavenger lands and the Wyld Hunt isn't as effective as elsewhere, and in general there are a lot of places where you aren't ostracized after Exalting, like pretty much anywhere not directly sharing a shoreline with the Realm.<br /> <br /> Exalted is meant to share human interactions, not as much as say Chuubo maybe but still you are meant to talk to people, so why not family and neighbors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T02:10:59-07:00","id":980164,"title":"","content":"A general comment to players: Don't let poor experiences from one ST punish another ST by tying their hands with regards to doing interesting things with your character because you have bad ST PTSD. Or PBSTSD. Post Bad Storyteller Stress Disorder. That includes &quot;defending&quot; a character by making their background sparse or made with a siege mentality. A game takes a group effort, and that includes investment and a reasonable expectation that you trust the ST.<br /> <br /> One of the things that helps discourage this kind of chargen behavior is a strong session 0 and a &quot;Justify your dots&quot; mentality as a Storyteller. Having players explaining character dots in a satisfactory in-universe manner often forces people to imply they had training or relationships with others to acquire skills or abilities. I am open to PM's telling me about how I'm a terrible ST for doing this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T02:34:15-07:00","id":980167,"title":"","content":"Me and my group, for player characters, basically 'interview' our own characters. We write out 20 to 100 questions, and answer them, really getting a good feel for the character. Other players don't get to see them, of course, but are given to the Storyteller for study and inclusion into the game.<br /> <br /> Its worked pretty well and has developed much more believable characters in our experience so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T02:43:54-07:00","id":980170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980164#post980164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A general comment to players: Don't let poor experiences from one ST punish another ST by tying their hands with regards to doing interesting things with your character because you have bad ST PTSD. Or PBSTSD. Post Bad Storyteller Stress Disorder. That includes &quot;defending&quot; a character by making their background sparse or made with a siege mentality. A game takes a group effort, and that includes investment and a reasonable expectation that you trust the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's as bad to the player as I've heard some people say, what amounts to &quot;just get over it&quot; isn't going to cut it.<br /> <br /> It's honestly much easier of the system itself discourages or bars that kind of GM/ST abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T02:45:37-07:00","id":980171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980170#post980170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's as bad to the player as I've heard some people say, what amounts to &quot;just get over it&quot; isn't going to cut it.<br /> <br /> It's honestly much easier of the system itself discourages or bars that kind of GM/ST abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re-read my post.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T02:53:11-07:00","id":980173,"title":"","content":"I can't help but notice that there are three recent threads complaining about how players create and play their characters. All started by Eldagusto. Isn't that interesting?<br /> <br /> My signature PC is close to his family, which is his father, mother, brother, and sister. He is also close to the other members of his father's war band. He uses his power to advance the interests of his family, his clan, his tribe, and his homeland.<br /> <br /> I can see why players would opt to play orphans or otherwise be disconnected from their families, though. Being Exalted is supposed to come with a host of issues, and among them is often rejection by your family - and everyone who has ever known you, really, as word spreads. Also, a Circle going on adventures means that you're probably going to be spending a <i>lot</i> of time away from family. It's often easier for the player to ignore or write off the question of family altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T02:56:21-07:00","id":980174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980171#post980171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Re-read my post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did, nothing changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T03:04:24-07:00","id":980177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980170#post980170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's as bad to the player as I've heard some people say, what amounts to &quot;just get over it&quot; isn't going to cut it.<br /> <br /> It's honestly much easier of the system itself discourages or bars that kind of GM/ST abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>No system can protect a player from a dick GM. The social contract is supposed to. If your GM doesn't respect the social contract, replace the GM.<br /> <br /> What ParanoiaCombo is saying is that you shouldn't hold the crimes of bad GMs against all GMs.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you're saying, though. Why <i>can't</i> a player just &quot;get over it&quot; with a new GM? Is every player that has ever played with a dick GM suffering from PTSD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T04:30:47-07:00","id":980191,"title":"","content":"While my Zenith Caste character idea (who my avatar is a picture of, in fact) is an orphan, she's got the priestesses who took her in and raised her as a surrogate family, so narratively that doesn't count IMO. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, my Dusk Caste is an orphan- in fact, her entire village was slaughtered in the event leading to her Exaltation- but her story is intended to be about redemption and rebuilding a life from nothing, so t fits there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T05:42:18-07:00","id":980202,"title":"","content":"I'm currently playing a character that thought she was an orphan till a few sessions ago. It was a deal with my GM to surprise me what he would do with her family. She needed to have her wings from somewhere and since she isn't a wyld mutant that only leaves a godblooded father. She is currently trying to find out more about her family that she thought had abandoned her. <br /> Well and here comes the thing why I wouldn't do that again. It seems like she is part of a 300 hundred soul strong breed of winged half-gods born only to be part of a mass-suicide bombing squad against the realm. Since the Scarlett Empress disappeared it seems like the suicide squad got abandoned. <br /> <br /> <br /> The GM has a very cruel side sometimes. Same happened to the family of a different character and player. He left because he exalted and wanted to protect them by not being there. They got murdered and tormented from an outcast of the realm. <br /> The whole village of my last character fell victim to the army of Mask Of Winters while my character was out far in the west adventuring in the name of Fakharu. <br /> The next character was kicked out of his tribe because of his Exaltation, because I didn't want to deal with this again. <br /> My first Vampire character got his new life only through the fall and slaughtering of his whole noble house that got eradicated through the intrigues of a different family. He was the last one left alive. (All of it was planned from my former GM) <br /> <br /> <br /> So I can understand why people don't want to have families ingame. Either they are cruel and antagonists that nobody really wants to have, or they get cruely murdered anyway without the chance of doing anything to prevent it. Revenge in one form or the other is pretty much the only story I ever experienced being told with the family in the center. <br /> That pretty much sums up my experience with families in RPGs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally I don't like this at all. I feel like it is a hassel. Important play time that is not wasted but that could be spent better on so many other things.<br /> The group I'm GMing in would never have to deal with stuff like this except when the players ask for it. Even when they fuck up ingame I don't just let the family get slaughtered. Even if they are antagonists they are so while being torn apart on the inside or having other reasons than hate and madness. Also family does not need to be rescued every freaking time. They are actually allowed to not die and be awesome themself! It's not like some people wouldn't be motivated to be a better version of themself if a Solar pops up within their bloodline. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T06:50:52-07:00","id":980220,"title":"","content":"Exalted is about larger-than-life. It's lame to see the same old cliches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like my Avatar? Courtesy of<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Jen</span>! : <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anybody want their characters to be experimented on ? </span>post 98<br /> <i>An Exalt is never unarmed.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4018-l-het-esh","name":"L'het'esh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:10:25-07:00","id":980248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980177#post980177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No system can protect a player from a dick GM.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is very true.<br /> <br /> Which makes it sad that there are players which expect a system to protect them from a dick GM, usually because of the self-fulfilling prophecy that is believing there is unlikely or difficult to find (or create/become) a replacement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980177#post980177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What ParanoiaCombo is saying is that you shouldn't hold the crimes of bad GMs against all GMs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly agree with that thought.<br /> <br /> I've actually got a couple players in my group right now that put the whole group in a sucky position when it comes to deciding what game to play. For example, everyone in the group is interested in playing magic-wielding characters living in secret amidst the modern world, but one player refuses to play Mage (both the Ascension and the Awakening) because he played it back in the day with a GM and set of players that have long since been kicked out of the group because they just plain suck to play with and didn't like it. So we just can't play that thing we are all, and yes that's even the guy that won't play Mage, interested in because we have to choose between playing Mage without him, or playing one of the many other games we are all interested in with him (and feel like we're the ones being unreasonable if we actually choose Mage in that situation).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:34:19-07:00","id":980257,"title":"","content":"I've been gaming for 25ish years. I've had more family &amp; friend based plots than I care to count and they are all based on the same thing. An essentially random NPC gets railroaded into a dangerous situation and I have to save or avenge them. The problem is, unless this is an NPC that has been brought to life by the GM through serious roleplaying, my character cares but I don't anymore. If the GM brought him/her to life, its no longer an NPC from my backstory and indistinguishable from any other major NPC. The only seperator is that I wrote a few lines of rough description at some point, the rest is the GM. <br /> <br /> Frankly, I don't get what the big deal is. Background ties are a very hand-wavey thing. Without the GM investing a serious amount of work into it, they are basically a McGuffin. Either the GM invests into shaping the rough outline of the player or he shapes his own NPC. I don't see much of a difference here.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the time spend shoehorning in family against the player's wishes could be spend developing &quot;normal&quot; NPC ties with the added bonus of allowing the player a choice to care. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980164#post980164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A general comment to players: Don't let poor experiences from one ST punish another ST by tying their hands with regards to doing interesting things with your character because you have bad ST PTSD. Or PBSTSD. Post Bad Storyteller Stress Disorder. That includes &quot;defending&quot; a character by making their background sparse or made with a siege mentality. A game takes a group effort, and that includes investment and a reasonable expectation that you trust the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Statements like these make me angry to be honest. Player's don't &quot;punish&quot; the new GM. They try to avoid a situation in which they are uncomfortably emotionally involved during their free time. They want their fun to be fun, not distressing.<br /> <br /> Trust is a fragile thing that needs to be earned. Dealing with emotionally distressing situations in RPGs is not a given. Its something that players and GM need to be okay with. A player that tries to &quot;defend&quot; himself, as you put it, against that is someone whose trust you need to earn by showing him that you won't abuse his emotional ties in horrible ways. Asking a scarred player to just forget what made him not have fun and making himself vulnerable all over again, with nothing but your word to go on, is a bad way to do that.<br /> <br /> Players open up to well crafted NPCs. It's a natural process. If they don't, its because they don't want to. Personally, I think the question why is much more interessting than blanket blaming the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10990-beaumis","name":"Beaumis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T10:47:29-07:00","id":980332,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.<br /> <br /> Lessee... Current and former Exalted characters...<ul><li>Heaven's Reach Battles was already elderly when she exalted; she'd been married to her work and had no children, and had outlived any parents or siblings.</li> <li>Chirpy Twilight Beatstick was born in a poor farming family, who gave her up to a local monastic order as an alternative to infanticide of a kid they <i>could not</i> afford to raise. Both family and order are safe... someplace else.</li> <li>Assassin's Creed Night <i>is</i> an orphan and is doing the Revenge Plot thing.</li> <li>Dawn Cataphract <i>thought</i> she was an orphan for some years, but has turned out to be wrong, which is a major plot point. Her mother is now an Exigent, and she has one maternal (majorly God-blooded) and two paternal (Abyssal and Fire Aspect, respectively) half-siblings, as well as an adult niece and nephew from a third paternal half-sib.</li> <li>Zenith Showoff is a world-traveler who stopped coming home to the boring village that she was born in when she realized that she and her kin no longer had sufficient common experiences to be mutually intelligible. Her romantic situation is <i>more</i> than complicated enough to make up for this.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T10:56:34-07:00","id":980339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980177#post980177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No system can protect a player from a dick GM. The social contract is supposed to. If your GM doesn't respect the social contract, replace the GM.</div> </div> </div> </div>A system can help by discouraging that behavior in the very way play is conducted. It can't stop it (and saying &quot;bar it&quot; was on me, my fault), but it <b>can</b> help. That's what I wanted to say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980177#post980177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What ParanoiaCombo is saying is that you shouldn't hold the crimes of bad GMs against all GMs.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you're saying, though. Why <i>can't</i> a player just &quot;get over it&quot; with a new GM? Is every player that has ever played with a dick GM suffering from PTSD?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have any direct experience with PTSD (I have my own mental illnesses), but I see at least some connection with people who perform the kind of bad play we're talking about. Protecting their characters by not having any connection with the world including family or friends. Turtling up by refusing to do anything that their characters aren't &quot;good&quot; at and only engaging in unambiguous victories. Constantly back-pedaling every and anything they do that would even slightly inconvenience them because they're so afraid of being bitten in the ass.<br /> <br /> And yet, those people keep coming back, even if they're not having fun. Because they <b>want</b> to have fun but they don't know how.<br /> <br /> Players who perform bad play out of fear don't do it because they're dicks. They do so because that's what they learned. And unlearning takes time and effort, and if supposedly &quot;good&quot; GMs aren't willing to provide that, then that's their business. They're not obligated to care in any way they don't want to. But they also don't get off just telling those players with bad experiences written directly in their play to &quot;get over it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11538,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","user":"kingcrackers","date":". 10-02-2016, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:56:47-07:00","id":980392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980339#post980339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A system can help by discouraging that behavior in the very way play is conducted. It can't stop it (and saying &quot;bar it&quot; was on me, my fault), but it <b>can</b> help. That's what I wanted to say.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't have any direct experience with PTSD (I have my own mental illnesses), but I see at least some connection with people who perform the kind of bad play we're talking about. Protecting their characters by not having any connection with the world including family or friends. Turtling up by refusing to do anything that their characters aren't &quot;good&quot; at and only engaging in unambiguous victories. Constantly back-pedaling every and anything they do that would even slightly inconvenience them because they're so afraid of being bitten in the ass.<br /> <br /> And yet, those people keep coming back, even if they're not having fun. Because they <b>want</b> to have fun but they don't know how.<br /> <br /> Players who perform bad play out of fear don't do it because they're dicks. They do so because that's what they learned. And unlearning takes time and effort, and if supposedly &quot;good&quot; GMs aren't willing to provide that, then that's their business. They're not obligated to care in any way they don't want to. But they also don't get off just telling those players with bad experiences written directly in their play to &quot;get over it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who has had dick GMs before, and also as someone who has replaced a dick GM, the road to recovery isn't as long as it sounds.<br /> <br /> Step 1. As the new GM, you talk to the players about what it is about past games that you feel were lacking, overly antagonistic, or otherwise bad for the experience, and promises to avoid these things.<br /> <br /> Step 2. Ask players to inform you of how they envision their character's story progressing, and work with them to integrate that. Specifically mention that if there's any aspect that they'd like to pursue, but didn't feel comfortable in previous games, for whatever reason, such as family ties, you would honor that and integrate it POSITIVELY into the plot as much as you're able. Rescue and/or revenge plots are viable, but only if specifically requested by the relevant player. Possibly offer additional character resources, like Solar XP, for receipt of the idea. Not when you get around to addressing it in-game, because that means the currently featured character is getting both game focus and character sheet rewards that the other characters currently aren't.<br /> <br /> Step 3. Take what you're offered. Do what you promised.<br /> <br /> Step 4. Watch as players respond to positive reinforcement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T14:40:21-07:00","id":980434,"title":"","content":"My current group has;<br /> <br /> \u2022 Dawn brawler, orphan, raised in the fighting pits of Nexus. Left when his adoptive 'parent' turned out to work for the mob and was fixing bouts. Seeking glory of his own. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Zenith northern tribesman; has a family and wife back home (except that his wife went missing in a snowstorm) and is traveling down in the hundred kingdoms looking for a guy to pass on memories to. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Twilight from a lost tribe of Demi-humans that have beeen barely surviving out in the Wyld. Strong sense of family/tribe commitment and is in creation looking for parts to fix the cauldron engine his people are living in. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Dawn martial artist. From a Beastman tribe that had been almost wiped out by 'soldiers in red armour'. She later discovered that the soldiers had sold her people to a raksha and they are all soul-bitten before being sold to the guild to work as slaves. She is trying to round them all up and get them back. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Eclipse beuracrat. Running from her family commitments on the blessed isle and trying to find a way to postpone or annul the engagement to a rising star Cathak general without sending her family into a debt they can never repay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T18:51:34-07:00","id":980511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980173#post980173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but notice that there are three recent threads complaining about how players create and play their characters. All started by Eldagusto. Isn't that interesting?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry did I just break a rule. Gee wiz I didn't realize we were not allowed to critically think about perceived foibles and bring them to light in a public forum as a subject of discussion. My gosh I can't believe I made such a faux pas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:09:33-07:00","id":980544,"title":"","content":"Kidnapping was a bad example. Here are some other examples:<br /> <br /> &gt; PC comes home and finds her family harassed by bandits/mob/etc. PC takes care of it.<br /> &gt; PC comes home and finds that her family business is failing. Her mother is getting old an senile. PC works with estranged sibling to make peace between mother and sibling.<br /> &gt; PC hears about father's death. Comes home to participate in funeral rituals. Deals with family drama and may find some problem in his home town to fix.<br /> &gt; PC's sister made a deal with some bad people. PC has to help her get out of it.<br /> &gt; PC's brother is trying to start up a new business. PC helps out in getting things off the ground.<br /> <br /> Two things I should note:<br /> <br /> 1) I don't force players to make characters with family. Not all role players want to deal with family drama. I do like my characters to at least think about their childhood and have some connection grounding them to the setting, but that can be beliefs/organizations/etc.<br /> <br /> 2) I always talk such plot over with the player before hand. I'm not going to drop family drama on the player out of the blue. I have GMs drop family plot on me out of the blue and that is not fun (&quot;Wow, thanks for creating a rapist father for my lost cub werewolf character without consulting me&quot;). I'm going to be &quot;okay, you are visiting your character's home town. What would you like to do there?&quot; &quot;I want my character to deal with his father's funeral&quot; &quot;Okay, I can work with that&quot; I also am not going to kill off family members unless the player agrees to it. Anyways killing off intimacies destroys the chance for future story lines.<br /> <br /> I like including slice of life scenes in Exalted to keep these god like character grounded and human. Yet at the same time, not all role players want to deal with slice of life scenes, which is perfectly fine too.<br /> <br /> My old Exalted game like them. We used to do funny training montages even though we didn't need to do them. Our Night Caste was doing resistance training and his teacher poisoned him. The Dusk and I made fun of him as he was puking in the bucket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 10-02-2016, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:47:39-07:00","id":980557,"title":"","content":"Basically, I make my characters orphans when it makes sense for them. Chiyoko's an orphan because it explains how she grew up in an order of shrine maiden-like priestesses. Blossom's an orphan because she lost everything, pretty much, in the course of her Exaltation. <br /> <br /> My Twilight, other Zenith, and Eclipse character ideas all have at least one parent left alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:50:17-07:00","id":980558,"title":"","content":"The Division of Endings retains a Family-Eating Consultant, whose duties center on guiding prospective heroes and historic figures towards the path of glory by murdering their parents. That explains it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T21:25:57-07:00","id":980573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980511#post980511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry did I just break a rule. Gee wiz I didn't realize we were not allowed to critically think about perceived foibles and bring them to light in a public forum as a subject of discussion. My gosh I can't believe I made such a faux pas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thou Shalt Not Criticize How Others Play the Game, because Their Preferences are not Your Preferences, Their Experiences are not Your Experiences, and Their Fun is not Your Fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T21:51:55-07:00","id":980579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980511#post980511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry did I just break a rule. Gee wiz I didn't realize we were not allowed to critically think about perceived foibles and bring them to light in a public forum as a subject of discussion. My gosh I can't believe I made such a faux pas.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you begin three threads in rapid succession with topics that seem to be variations of &quot;Are all players so terrabad at roleplaying?&quot;, then people will start wondering what's causing you to vent.<br /> <br /> Nothing big. Just an amused raised eyebrow.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 10-03-2016, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T22:55:41-07:00","id":980590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980579#post980579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you begin three threads in rapid succession with topics that seem to be variations of &quot;Are all players so terrabad at roleplaying?&quot;, then people will start wondering what's causing you to vent.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Cool Story Bros. Three threads in a five day period of time, with two of them posted right before I went to sleep... yeah that is just incessant, I am just flooding the whole forums aren't I? <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;Are all players so terrabad at roleplaying?&quot;, yeah that is what I am doing when I post three threads were people are civilly discussing actually experiences, and discuss subjects pertaining to ongoing and previous games, where the three questions are, one pertaining to diversity (in a gameline that is trying to blaze the trail with making diversity acceptable), one about a regular cliche of people being orphans too often, and the last about advice on making connections for pcs when starting a game... yeah you clearly are not trying to spin a narrative or strawman everything.<br /> <br /> Look the thread titles were made to be tongue in cheek, most people seem to get that. Its been pretty civil so far, regardless of people trying to fake coyness when slighting me for posting these discussions. An Author and Moderators are even posting, no threats from them or red Mod Voices, so clearly they are being tricked and these threads are wicked wicked things.<br /> <br /> Telling me not to discuss these subjects civilly is closer to you blokes breaking the rules then me I'm afraid. I've not told people they can't do things in their own game, and I was even asking advice for myself. I popped in two new players and one of the players is very... DnD in his mindset, so I thought to look inward on past experiences and discuss some things I just thought of.<br /> <br /> I sense a LOT of people projecting their own strange little issues onto other people here when people have been pretty productive and have been pretty on ball with discussions. So while I do appreciate people trying to derail and stop these three threads, may I suggest if you don't like them being discussed you don't need to post on them. If you want to discuss these subjects please post I am listening.<br /> <br /> <br /> Grrr... my first typing got eaten and had to retype.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T22:57:13-07:00","id":980592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980573#post980573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thou Shalt Not Criticize How Others Play the Game, because Their Preferences are not Your Preferences, Their Experiences are not Your Experiences, and Their Fun is not Your Fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Broham you are the one doing this trying to bully me into not having a simple discussion. People are just talking, chillax no one is trying to dictate anything. Though I am getting some... threadcrapping vibes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:09:20-07:00","id":980595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980592#post980592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Broham you are the one doing this trying to bully me into not having a simple discussion. People are just talking, chillax no one is trying to dictate anything. Though I am getting some... threadcrapping vibes...</div> </div> </div> </div>I contributed to the discussion. I just also happened to observe that you've started several threads complaining about gamers in general being somehow lacking because they might not play in exactly your preferred way. That's more than a little rude, even if we've chosen to pick up the ball and run with it rather than take offense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:20:59-07:00","id":980600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980595#post980595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I contributed to the discussion. I just also happened to observe that you've started several threads complaining about gamers in general being somehow lacking because they might not play in exactly your preferred way. That's more than a little rude, even if we've chosen to pick up the ball and run with it rather than take offense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes once again you are trying to spin things...<br /> <br /> I did appreciate it when you posted contributing, less appreciative of the snideness and trying to raise up peoples cackles. I'm not even complaining in the Character connection thread.<br /> <br /> Super cool you're trying to speak for others, and define other peoples context.<br /> <br /> Pick up the ball and run with it... that is a very presumptious statement. And I find you rather rude in the execution of your intentions, meanwhile you are arguing I don't have a right to make three particular threads, and are trying to inflate a situation. Please report things to the moderator. Clearly people shouldn't ask each other how to improve their own games. That's one step above the usual fair, I shouldn't even ask how to improve my own game, or ask about experiences...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:29:02-07:00","id":980604,"title":"","content":"In general, yeah, there is a certain feeling that mortal parents just drag you down, maaaan. I was actively told I was doing it wrong for making a Lunar whose primary preoccupation was making sure her family was well off and safe, because that is apparently not proper Exalted narrative. Exalts shouldn't be caring about something as &quot;small and inconsequential&quot; as a mortal cobbler and his wife, apparently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:28:37-07:00","id":980628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980600#post980600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes once again you are trying to spin things...<br /> <br /> I did appreciate it when you posted contributing, less appreciative of the snideness and trying to raise up peoples cackles. I'm not even complaining in the Character connection thread.<br /> <br /> Super cool you're trying to speak for others, and define other peoples context.<br /> <br /> Pick up the ball and run with it... that is a very presumptious statement. And I find you rather rude in the execution of your intentions, meanwhile you are arguing I don't have a right to make three particular threads, and are trying to inflate a situation. Please report things to the moderator. Clearly people shouldn't ask each other how to improve their own games. That's one step above the usual fair, I shouldn't even ask how to improve my own game, or ask about experiences...</div> </div> </div> </div>You have the right, sure. No one said you didn't. Being rude isn't prohibited. What you're doing, however, is repeatedly objecting to the characters that other people choose to play. Which is <i>very</i> rude. How many times, in my years of mostly-lurking, have I seen the fundamental themes repeated? What works for my group at my table to have fun isn't wrong. What works for your group at your table to have fun isn't wrong. These are not necessarily the same things, other people are not wrong for not conforming to your expectations.<br /> <br /> If people don't care to explore family-related ideas at the table, that's up to them. If people want to roleplay meeting, as opposed to the game starting after they've met, that's up to them. The race people choose to roleplay as is up to them. If it works at their table and everyone's fine with it, YOU don't get to criticize them for that. Yet, those three threads are inherently critical in the OP of other players for not sharing your views.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:51:27-07:00","id":980634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980628#post980628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have the right, sure. No one said you didn't. Being rude isn't prohibited. What you're doing, however, is repeatedly objecting to the characters that other people choose to play. Which is <i>very</i> rude. How many times, in my years of mostly-lurking, have I seen the fundamental themes repeated? What works for my group at my table to have fun isn't wrong. What works for your group at your table to have fun isn't wrong. These are not necessarily the same things, other people are not wrong for not conforming to your expectations.<br /> <br /> If people don't care to explore family-related ideas at the table, that's up to them. If people want to roleplay meeting, as opposed to the game starting after they've met, that's up to them. The race people choose to roleplay as is up to them. If it works at their table and everyone's fine with it, YOU don't get to criticize them for that. Yet, those three threads are inherently critical in the OP of other players for not sharing your views.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said you can't use the Orphan route, you've been places words, intentions, and context in my mouth the whole time. Nobody is telling you how to run your game. I even friggin mentioned how currently my group is composed of Orphans. You trying to find a feud where there isn't one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:03:30-07:00","id":980638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980634#post980634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said you can't use the Orphan route, you've been places words, intentions, and context in my mouth the whole time. Nobody is telling you how to run your game. I even friggin mentioned how currently my group is composed of Orphans. You trying to find a feud where there isn't one.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan#post979475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <b>Seriously is every friggin Solar an Orphan?</b><br /><br /> </span><br /> </span></span><br /> </span><br /> </span><br /> <br /> <br /> Okay in my games, with Exalted Especially, players always want to make Oprhans. Yeah I get RPGs are escapism and allows people to avoid all the baggage of Family that they have in the real world, but in my current Game everyone is an Orphan, well almost, one player last minute changed his character from family lost to a bandit attack, to nah he left in his teens.<br /> <br /> And even more rare I never have anyone play someone who is married, but I guess that is probably because I've had experience playing games as a young person and also playing with fellow youths.<br /> <br /> But I've done things like incentivize people towards the vulnerability of family and friends by giving them bonuses like EXP at character creation. Because that seems to be the only damn way to get a group of non-hobo orphans.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a complaint, and thus, implied criticism, to me. The thread title uses language and structure usually implying exasperation. Let's see... then, you talk about the way people in your games tend to avoid family entanglements... and then, you talk about offering incentives to the contrary. &quot;Because that seems to be the only damn way to get a group of non-hobo orphans.&quot;<br /> <br /> It sure seems like you're talking about a player behavior you don't like that you're trying to &quot;fix.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:07:42-07:00","id":980642,"title":"","content":"Dude I said earlier these are all tongue in cheek exaggerated titles, I've been doing that around here for over a decade. And the exasperation comes in when literally everyone is an orphan. Clearly I don't have as big an issue as you seem to think because I allow everyone to choose such a background. But I wanted at least someone to ground the group into a territory and family or close friends would do that.<br /> <br /> Don't read to much into things. This was made to be a fun little discussion, no one is bashing you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:12:28-07:00","id":980645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980642#post980642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude I said earlier these are all tongue in cheek exaggerated titles, I've been doing that around here for over a decade. And the exasperation comes in when literally everyone is an orphan. Clearly I don't have as big an issue as you seem to think because I allow everyone to choose such a background. But I wanted at least someone to ground the group into a territory and family or close friends would do that.<br /> <br /> Don't read to much into things. This was made to be a fun little discussion, no one is bashing you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, if you're exaggerating for effect, fair enough I guess. I don't read these forums that often, and if this is a Thing You Do... I don't really get the joke... but sure, why not?<br /> <br /> It's my preference that characters have family connections too. They make for great stories and some of my favorite characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:18:52-07:00","id":980650,"title":"","content":"Can we get back to talking about the interesting discussion and not whether Eldagusto was right to make the interesting discussion please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:26:05-07:00","id":980653,"title":"","content":"Okay so sometimes I feel I tip to whenever I add relatives to a players character. Like I don't want to define them in a way they don't like so I rarely will add direct relatives but I feel uncles and cousins are more fair game.<br /> <br /> And do some people get upset if they make an orphan and you revel secret family? I guess it depends on the situation, you won't probably enjoy it if as mentioned by someone you make their dad a rapist Black Spiral Dancer or something and not consult them, but making them into an obstacle or villain is intriguing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:30:42-07:00","id":980654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980653#post980653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so sometimes I feel I tip to whenever I add relatives to a players character. Like I don't want to define them in a way they don't like so I rarely will add direct relatives but I feel uncles and cousins are more fair game.<br /> <br /> And do some people get upset if they make an orphan and you revel secret family? I guess it depends on the situation, you won't probably enjoy it if as mentioned by someone you make their dad a rapist Black Spiral Dancer or something and not consult them, but making them into an obstacle or villain is intriguing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding family to a player's character is... kind of a gray area, and I'd definitely want to talk it over with them before I pulled the trigger. What you're doing is changing their character by fiat, without their permission. There's not exactly a roll they can make to resist their character's family dynamic being retconned by the GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T02:48:35-07:00","id":980677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980650#post980650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we get back to talking about the interesting discussion and not whether Eldagusto was right to make the interesting discussion please?</div> </div> </div> </div>This please. Thanks everyone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T03:46:20-07:00","id":980692,"title":"","content":"I only just realised that my last character is an orphan, but I think orphan works because people with decent, whole families and regular dayjobs don't necessarily seek out adventure, which is something of a barrier to exaltation (although one of my current circle has a half-blood ape wife and went back to his office job after exalting and just hoped no-one would notice). Generally, if I don't specify parents/siblings/aunts and uncles/grandparents then my ST is free, within reason, to do what they like with them, and so am I. For instance, if we roll into a town and I've got a dot in Contacts, I'll weave Aunt Ciocia into the town and we'll go visit her, rather than approaching Contact #3346, but if we do, my ST is more than welcome to tell us that Uncle Wujek hasn't come back from his trip one village over, and start a little adventure.<br /> <br /> P.S I realised while writing this that we don't have a joint-noun for aunts and uncles like we do for most other familial connections. Apparently nieces and nephews are &quot;niblings&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T04:20:52-07:00","id":980699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980628#post980628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being rude isn't prohibited</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You should probably re-read the first three forum rules. If people continue to be rudely argumentative then those rules will be enforced.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:12:16-07:00","id":980723,"title":"","content":"We are getting two new players that never have played Exalted before and they are currently filling their character sheets and developing their background. So far we have one orphan, a night caste that grew up on the streets and one genius but abandoned strategist comming from an unimportant Gent of the Realm. <br /> <br /> I think it is quite interesting that both have cut their family ties or got their ties cut. Same goes for every other character in our group except for one, but for her it is a major story point to discover that she actually has a family and nobody knows if she is likes them or gets to be liked by them.<br /> <br /> As somebody already said, families can be emotionally taxing but for our group it seems like it's just easier to get into the adventure where nobody knows what to expect. Traveling is much easier if you don't have ties to important characters that have to stay put in some place to keep their lives going. Traveling and most importantly fighting with a Solar is almost always a free death card somewhere down the line. I guess nobody wants to have a size 1 family battlegroup. <br /> <br /> So I guess making families a regular part of the game that isn't just some typical go rescue or avenge type of quest requires a certain setup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:19:28-07:00","id":980727,"title":"","content":"I've noticed this in basically every sort of RPG I've ever played in.<br /> <br /> For example, a D&amp;D campaign I'm currently part of has 3 of the 4 characters either having no family...or their family is on the far end of the continent where they can't be involved in the game at all. The exception is my character, who has a very large family and interacts with them on a regular basis. My fellow players all stared at my like I'd grown a second head when I told them that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:44:57-07:00","id":980833,"title":"","content":"Never really worried about the subject - family and such will be a big thing to some character concepts (moses-style tribal/spiritual leader figure, scion of a northern city-state exiled for turning anathema and possible, spurious, ties to either fae or undead raiders, adventurous sijanese farmgirl that runns away from marriage to the local yeddim herder and becomes a mercenary soldier and eventually lieutenant under an outcaste captain) and meaningless to others (a number of PCs that were slaves of some kind at some point or other of their lives but managed to run away before or during their exaltations, or just characters living in directions almost opposite of their homelands for a variety of reasons), so i would say it depends on context or style.<br /> <br /> As long as the PCs provide you some juicy hooks to let you better understand what kind of stuff they would like to see more of, family or lack of it is secondary. One's past or ties can always be developed or form as the game moves forward. Lovers may appear, brothers and sisters, known, unknown, illegitimate or neomah-spawned, may rear their heads in unexpected contexts and so on, if there's use and/or entertainment value for that in one's story, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T11:19:49-07:00","id":980900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980699#post980699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You should probably re-read the first three forum rules. If people continue to be rudely argumentative then those rules will be enforced.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>What is the correct avenue to complain about moderation double-standards? I notice that this forum's &quot;Trouble Tickets&quot; section is only for technical issues, not administrative ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:12:25-07:00","id":980933,"title":"","content":"Aaaand.... back on topic... sort of. I usually take the stance that players should explain to me why they're out adventuring. In my current game, I have one player who has a wife and kid (who is, weirdly enough, my wife irl), one player who's character comes from a noble family far away, and one player who's character is a monk.<br /> <br /> The first player took the wife as Ally and the child as a flaw so the wife is actually helpful in the adventures and the kid, while troublesome, is a source of XP. The second player explained why his character was sent away from their kingdom. The last player invented an order who generally requires it's monks to not focus on their family attachments. So what I find helpful to keep everyone from being an orphan is get the players to actually come up with a reason for their adventuring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:31:21-07:00","id":980943,"title":"","content":"I should also note, that while your character's family may be in a completely different direction than you, they could still impact your character's life. An NPC may remind a character of their mother. They may have a goal of &quot;make being a solar socially acceptable, so I can go home.&quot; They may send money home, even though it is risky. They may hate their family and do things that destroy the family's slave business. Or they live by the morals instilled into them by their dear old Wandering Monk uncle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:14:05-07:00","id":981014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980692#post980692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.S I realised while writing this that we don't have a joint-noun for aunts and uncles like we do for most other familial connections. Apparently nieces and nephews are &quot;niblings&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... They're your parents' siblings, so... piblings!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1551-barefoot-monkey","name":"Barefoot Monkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1551_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T14:44:36-07:00","id":981030,"title":"","content":"It's actually a bit of a joke in my group. &quot;And how did <i>your</i> parents tragically die?&quot;<br /> <br /> Though I just learned that one of the solars in the game I'm running still has a mom hanging around somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9749-andrew-d","name":"Andrew D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:42:06-07:00","id":981171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980900#post980900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the correct avenue to complain about moderation double-standards? I notice that this forum's &quot;Trouble Tickets&quot; section is only for technical issues, not administrative ones.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bIf you took my suggestion about reading the forum rules you would see the correct procedure. Use the &quot;contact us&quot; link posted in those very rules.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:02:08-07:00","id":981188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=980943#post980943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should also note, that while your character's family may be in a completely different direction than you, they could still impact your character's life. An NPC may remind a character of their mother. They may have a goal of &quot;make being a solar socially acceptable, so I can go home.&quot; They may send money home, even though it is risky. They may hate their family and do things that destroy the family's slave business. Or they live by the morals instilled into them by their dear old Wandering Monk uncle.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, very true in all instances, thanks for bringing that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:28:07-07:00","id":981556,"title":"","content":"I have a group of five players who just got started and most of them didn't specify anything about their families when the made their backgrounds. Two mentioned family in their backgrounds but not their parents. We're doing flashbacks and such to fill in details so it is possible that most of them will have living parents by the time we're done with the early game establishing adventures.<br /> <br /> That's about right with my experiences; less that people are specifically orphans and more that they just don't think about who their parents are, beyond choosing which was which in cross breeding situations, i.e. a half elf, was the elf your mother or father?<br /> <br /> I genuinely wonder if it's a cultural thing. People often don't want to be defined by who their parents were in real life and I think that carries more is into fantasy escapism to the point that they don't want to even think about parents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:32:38-07:00","id":981783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Full Time GM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=981556#post981556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I genuinely wonder if it's a cultural thing. People often don't want to be defined by who their parents were in real life and I think that carries more is into fantasy escapism to the point that they don't want to even think about parents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's partially that, and partially that &quot;dead&quot; is a lot less grim than a lot of other possible outcomes, and that characters tend to be of an age, especially in most fantasy settings, where their parents would likely be dead. Why not make a tragic backstory of it, if they're going to be in the ground anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:34:10-07:00","id":981886,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I played an air aspected Dragon Blood named Cynis Diah in a 4 year long Exalted Campaign. Everybody else played Solars, but it was best game I ever played. In that game my family at least figured prominently. Nobody else had NPC\u2019s that figured into their character before game began. My PC was a little unusual in that despite being a member of house Cynis, he supported Solars. My father was none other than the crackpot inventor Cynis Mond and my mother was Lesser Elemental Dragon of Air. For the most part except for a single charm I was strictly a Dragonblood with a Breeding of 6. Largely my PC was an experiment to help purify the bloodlines of the house. My wife was a powerful sorcerer and a strong ally. I had several children. One to start and several more over the course of the 4 decades our game covered. My mother served as a potent liege and my father a strong mentor. Both characters while not commonly encountered were felt by me and the rest of my fellow players over the course of the game. I garnered concubines and followers all of whom had names and began to make up our large cast of supporting characters and I wasn\u2019t the only with the supporting cast, but I did have strong family ties.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:32:20-07:00","id":983631,"title":"","content":"But seriously, protagonists have been orphans for a lot longer than RPGs general existence, so I see no reason to NOT make my character an island before he meets the Party.<br /> <br /> What can I say, I'm a sap for the surrogate family spiel.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T19:32:53-07:00","id":983689,"title":"","content":"As an aside, playing a Dragon-blooded dynast or Gens scion with little to no family connections might be something of a challenge i guess, as their family support and infrastructure is kind of the point with DB lineages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T19:34:30-07:00","id":983692,"title":"","content":"I play Solars with lots of different family backgrounds. Some orphans, others with small nuclear families, others with large extended families. I usually go with whatever I feel fits the character.<br /> <br /> In one game I had an unfun family/close connections experience with an ST (not bagging on the ST, that one particular experience just wasn't fun for me). So for the game that immediately followed that one, I made a character as an orphan with no connections. Although the ST for that game was different I was so burnt out on the whole &quot;MWAHAHAHAHA! BEHOLD, HERO! I have your wife/kids/friends/lovers/favorite hunting hound/fuzziest adorable kitten!&quot; ploys and just didn't want to run the risk of the burnt out story line making an appearance in that campaign. So one of the new orphan character's major plot points was connecting with people and learning to love and trust others again. It was fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:43:39-07:00","id":983730,"title":"","content":"And of course, sometimes being an orphan does not stop your parents hanging around...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Honestly. I've been dead for nigh on twenty years now. When are you going to get it together and give me some grandbabies to haunt?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:46:56-07:00","id":983732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=983730#post983730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course, sometimes being an orphan does not stop your parents hanging around...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Honestly. I've been dead for nigh on twenty years now. When are you going to get it together and give me some grandbabies to haunt?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You are BRILLIANT!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T04:23:52-07:00","id":983847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=983730#post983730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course, sometimes being an orphan does not stop your parents hanging around...<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Honestly. I've been dead for nigh on twenty years now. When are you going to get it together and give me some grandbabies to haunt?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As one who has used ancestors for that and then some in the occasional game, i can certainly relate.<br /> <br /> In fact i have a specially entertaining case i enjoyed STing where the haunter <b>wasn't </b>a true blood relative, but its undead <i>godfather</i>, something that resulted from a promise made by the PC's parents after trespassing upon the tomb of a remnant from some long forgotten pre-contagion culture whose rest they disturbed, in exchange for sparing them and given with all the forethought one might expect from such a hasty and self-serving deal. Then months later the couple finds itself haunted not only by that ghost, but other haunts of those lost people, inspired to an unusual burst of communal activity and action by the idea of bringing his long-lost nation to a new form of existence in the living world through the patronage of a whole generation of godchildren. And so it was that they saw themselves pressured in having kids - and tricking a number of scavenger lords, wannabe adventurers and tomb-robbers into ending up in similar sort of deals with other leaders among the dead of Ozymandias of the Sands (subtle?me? what for...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T04:53:52-07:00","id":983853,"title":"","content":"I can't think of the signature Celestials who have parents.<br /> <br /> Agree with Wizard of Oz that having parents doesn't seem to be that common in the heroic narratives Exalted draws from - where was Elric's dad, or Conan's, or Fafhrd or Grey Mouser's, or Ged's?<br /> <br /> I kind of prefer the &quot;Mum and dad are around... but just not that important in my life. We're pretty independent you know.&quot; or &quot;My dad is a roguish con man, and we aren't exactly close, y'know, though our paths occasionally cross&quot; because those feels the route that I would expect most Exalted protags to take while avoiding the orphan cliche. I think in much of Exalted's world, people living close to their parents their whole life might be not always the most common thing. Usually your heroic protagonists are people who've been seeking their fortune and wider adventure, and that distances you from your upbringing a bit.<br /> <br /> Having parents in the frame could be cool though, a la Henry and Indy Jones or other tales. In lots pulp it might be easier than in Exalted to add in dad or mum, as a heroic figure who is a peer of the protagonist, because they could be fairly awesome in their own right, however Exalted for Celestials makes that less probable because it's not probable and somewhat against the theme of Celestials for the gods to favor many in the same family. So you'd have to work them in as a lesser heroic figure or an ordinary one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T06:57:44-07:00","id":983899,"title":"","content":"My Eclipse is a son of the Scarlet Empress","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T08:02:42-07:00","id":983923,"title":"","content":"Arianna grew up with her Father.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T11:17:26-07:00","id":983985,"title":"","content":"Speaking of signature solars...<br /> <br /> - <i>Dace</i>, i think, lived with his parents until he decided to run away as a youth for the adventurous life of a mercenary soldier.<br /> <br /> - <i>Swan</i>, while not much is said about them, most certainly had a pretty revelant family as he was part of the nobility of Coral and courting one daughter of its ruler before the chain of events that lead to his exaltation.<br /> <br /> - <i>Harmonious Jade</i> never knew her parents and was created from infancy as a salmalin assassin, while <i>Panther</i> seems to have been the child of unamed slaves or a prostitute and climbed from that pit by hand, tooth and nail (metaphorically <b>and</b> literally).<br /> <br /> - <i>Bull of the North</i> was already an old man that had outlived his second or third wife and witness the commemorative dance of his <b>grandaughter </b>for her first child, going through something like depression/mid-life crisis/survivor guilt because of it, when he decided to leave the tribe to die and was intead chosen by the UCS to be his holy engine of righteous war upon Creation. That said, little to nothing is said of these descendants afaik.<br /> <br /> Those are the ones i remember, i guess there are others tales and examples, but overall it's a big world and how proeminently does family figure or not a the hero or heroine's saga can vary considerably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-08-2016, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T11:32:55-07:00","id":983988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tenkage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=983899#post983899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Eclipse is a son of the Scarlet Empress</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an Eclipse who is the god-blooded son of Dreamweaver, one of the three big gods of Great Forks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T11:37:48-07:00","id":983991,"title":"","content":"I'd correct for Dace: &quot;It's no surprise that I became a mercenary - I grew up in the camps. Sergeant Redda told me that I joined the company after they hit a rebel town near Thorns. I was five or six at the time and don't remember much before then. My life was the Wolves&quot;. Orphan club?<br /> <br /> And add that Swan's a bit separated from his family by his service as a diplomat, so sort of falls for me into a category of being pretty independent from his parents and family (but no orphan).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T12:47:51-07:00","id":984015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=983991#post983991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd correct for Dace: &quot;It's no surprise that I became a mercenary - I grew up in the camps. Sergeant Redda told me that I joined the company after they hit a rebel town near Thorns. I was five or six at the time and don't remember much before then. My life was the Wolves&quot;. Orphan club?</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, it has been years since i last read most of the character backgrounds in the 1e castebooks (what is a damn shame in retrospect, as they are such great setting fodder) and must admit the Bull's tale always felt the most poignant, on its own and through sheer contrast with his usual image/portrayal in many other materials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=983991#post983991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And add that Swan's a bit separated from his family by his service as a diplomat, so sort of falls for me into a category of being pretty independent from his parents and family (but no orphan).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, his family background is sort of a given from his social position, but family relations not really delved upon.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T12:52:12-07:00","id":984018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=983730#post983730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course, sometimes being an orphan does not stop your parents hanging around...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Honestly. I've been dead for nigh on twenty years now. When are you going to get it together and give me some grandbabies to haunt?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an Abyssal concept where his grandmother's ghost is an ally. He is her last desendant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T15:06:02-07:00","id":984074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=983730#post983730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course, sometimes being an orphan does not stop your parents hanging around...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Honestly. I've been dead for nigh on twenty years now. When are you going to get it together and give me some grandbabies to haunt?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, we have Salt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T21:06:37-07:00","id":984223,"title":"","content":"Well, my character is not an orphan, His father is an Isidoric Akuma and his mother is an abyssal under lover clad (lover clad is his godmother xD).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T15:15:12-07:00","id":984614,"title":"","content":"If every Solar is an orphan, what happens when the child of two Solars is destined to become a Solar? :O<br /> <br /> No wonder there aren't Solar breeding camps. It'd be the fastest way to kill them ever.<br /> <br /> Pass me another couple of those cute little vodka bottles, I just ran dry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T02:19:19-07:00","id":984796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=983853#post983853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kind of prefer the &quot;Mum and dad are around... but just not that important in my life. We're pretty independent you know.&quot; or &quot;My dad is a roguish con man, and we aren't exactly close, y'know, though our paths occasionally cross&quot; because those feels the route that I would expect most Exalted protags to take while avoiding the orphan cliche.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bSure and many Exalted are going to be travellers under circumstances where that means you lose touch with your homeland forever, whether it's travelling to the big city because you're the third or fourth son and don't want to live as your brother's farm hand or crossing the ocean to take part in a colony. There aren't phones to keep in regular contact with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12512-whimsicalpigeon","name":"whimsicalpigeon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T02:26:04-07:00","id":984797,"title":"","content":"Overtly breaking off ties with family (or <i>pretending</i> to) in order to keep the wyld hunts from using them as bait is also an <i>in character</i> thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T10:46:58-08:00","id":1005407,"title":"","content":"Does it count when your mother was a badass sorceress killed by the Realm in your backstory, and your father is the Fetich Soul of the Demon City with whom she had a one-night-stand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T11:09:04-08:00","id":1005410,"title":"","content":"That definitely counts.<br /> <br /> Sounds neat, but totally counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T11:42:19-08:00","id":1005417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=1005407#post1005407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it count when your mother was a badass sorceress killed by the Realm in your backstory, and your father is the Fetich Soul of the Demon City with whom she had a one-night-stand?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends; has the demon actually contributed to raising you?<br /> <br /> After all, not all orphans have parents who are dead; some are simply abandoned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T11:56:16-08:00","id":1005422,"title":"","content":"not necesarily<br /> <br /> I've written up several solars without various flavors of family:<br /> <br /> The exiled prince/princess (gender of character not nailed down yet) - accidentally killed his/her brother during a sparring exercise. Is exiled, and ends up working for a mercenary company - exalts as a dawn caste. Name: The Would-Be King, with his army of Should-Have-Beens - and as a solar now... he would like his throne.<br /> <br /> The little girl from Great Forks was adopted into the local chapter of the Cult of the Illuminated, after her parents were murdered by another cult that saught to abduct the beautiful little girl for sexual exploits because pleasure cults have to get their child prostitutes somewhere - zenith caste 'no fun allowed' type who really likes to stamp out corrupt practices that are veiled behind religious ceremony and dogma. To her, the cult of the illuminated in great forks is her family.<br /> <br /> The Lookshyan retiree, former of combat medic of the first field force. Lives in a hinterland, but doesn't get along with the local magistrate because the magistrate is a blowhard while the old medic has been all over the east and seen enough to know that the magistrate's bullshit is nothing he needs to listen to. He is estranged from his family after his mother died of old age, when he refused to accept his brother's take-over of the family business because said brother is a shady fucker who then went on to ruin and bancrupt said business. Lot of bad blood there.<br /> <br /> each have unique family situations and ties - some good, some not so good, some open for exploitation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T13:51:38-08:00","id":1005466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=1005417#post1005417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends; has the demon actually contributed to raising you?<br /> <br /> After all, not all orphans have parents who are dead; some are simply abandoned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does sending you visions of his glory that impart sorcerous knowledge, leaving you an awesome reaper daiklave of malfean iron and orichalcum that will allow you to access the power of your infernal heritage through Evocations, and sending you a neomah concubine for your birthday count for contributions? Because if so Ligier is an awesome but distant father to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T13:58:04-08:00","id":1005467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=1005466#post1005466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does sending you visions of his glory that impart sorcerous knowledge, leaving you an awesome reaper daiklave of malfean iron and orichalcum that will allow you to access the power of your infernal heritage through Evocations, and sending you a neomah concubine for your birthday count for contributions? Because if so Ligier is an awesome but distant father to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems legit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T15:53:02-08:00","id":1005503,"title":"","content":"A solar concept I would like to see, would be a parent<br /> <br /> ...a Solar with children. Say, a mother - who then has to deal with the fact that her children are now more of a hindrance, targets for manipulative Sidereals and Abyssals - as is the rest of her family. Of course, she also loves her children, so she would never want to see them hurt or sent away while she does her Solar thing.<br /> <br /> Oh and her Lunar mate is crazy jealous of all this attention not being given to him/her... who may or may not be planning to perform a sacred hunt on her children, in order to become them... to get all of the Solar's attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T16:25:33-08:00","id":1005512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=1005503#post1005503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A solar concept I would like to see, would be a parent<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My current Eclipse is still hiding on the Blessed Isle because he couldn't leave his children behind. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T17:19:11-08:00","id":1005517,"title":"","content":"Our current circle is this<br /> Dawn: Family was killed by his Infernal rival in backstory, his fault after getting his tribe exiled from their ancestral home by angering the Island God. Big part of his motivation<br /> Zenith: Family not really brought up. We're in Palanquin and he is from the Blessed Isle so it is very likely he will never be able to see them again<br /> Night: Father was killed by a Ys Sorcerer. Mother is still a slave on the Island, big part of his motivation is to free her.Hates the fact that the circle has been working with the Ys against the Fair Folk<br /> Twilight: Her mother was a cloudfolk and they kept in touch. There wasn't much other mentioned other than her father was a mortal craftsman. I wrote up on the spot a personality for her mother when she went home for cloudstuff to make an artifact, Mother is super overbearing and really gets around, very racist against the 'Dirty people on the ground'. They care for each other a lot, everyone really enjoyed seeing our least socially capable circlemember in an embarrassing social situation. 10/10, would have overbearing mother figure telling twilight to go settle down again.<br /> <br /> A lot of time when this doesn't pop up, its with players who haven't really developed the character's needs, but want the game to move forward so they can roleplay stuff going on right now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T17:28:18-08:00","id":1005520,"title":"","content":"Overall, the question of Solars as orphans is interesting to me because it ties into the whole question of where any given Solar came from, and what they were doing in the world prior to being Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough it does make me think... whether they're sedentary or widely travelled, I imagine that a fair number of Solars aren't orphans in the strictest sense, but might also not have living parents, depending on how old they are and what the local age of mortality might be like.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the other hand, I think of a few backstories given in things like the Caste books which would feel like the kind of thing where you would expect parents to be around, but they're just kind of overlooked.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't know anything about most of the writers of those books, but I would still vaguely speculate that that may have more to do with lacking personal familiarity with the idea of being a mature adult whose parents still live a few houses over in more than a few cases.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough I'm also thinking about the example of somebody such as the Hongwu Emperor, who proclaimed himself at the age of about forty, annnnnnd no, his entire family died when he was 16. Hmm... maybe Emperor Gaozu of Han? I wonder what might have become of his parents and family, if they were still alive when he was in his fifties and rose to power.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt is interesting to consider the idea of a relatively young Solar who still lives at home and comes from a society with values of filial piety. That's one of those interesting situations in which somebody rises alongside somebody who acquires the power directly, like when the wife of a swineherd becomes Empress of Eastern Rome.<br /> <br /> \u200bNote to self; Solar who creates persona of dead parents in the hopes of capturing their personality to continue to advise and enact courses of action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T18:23:12-08:00","id":1005531,"title":"","content":"Sorta like <i>Cloak &amp; Dagger</i>, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T13:12:22-08:00","id":1006826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ketrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=979517#post979517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man. My group's poor Realmies probably WISH they were orphans. The Twilight's family obligations are a centerpiece of the plot, which focuses on the inter-House struggle for the ownership of a relatively wealthy Northern state that's within three months march of the Bull's warpath. I've got two actual orphans who are on opposite ends of the mood spectrum here. One is a typical wandering kung fu hobo, but the other was raised by a crime syndicate that shattered in a night of terror and fire. His Contacts rating is his scattered &quot;siblings&quot;, and they've come up two or three times into the story so far (11 sessions in). Most recently, one of them upped the stakes in a city the Circle &quot;liberated&quot; simply by being present and extremely pregnant. It gave him extra motivation to keep their little coup as bloodless as possible.<br /> <br /> With the exception of the kung fu hobo, all of my players have been drowning me in NPC attachments. It's honestly impossible to include them all. The same would be true even if they were all orphans, so I don't think the lack of parents is intrinsically problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost never have orphans in mine, unless it happens during game.<br /> <br /> One game I ST, characters' mother, a goddess, is alive and active in her life, and her &quot;family&quot; connections to the Unconquered Sun were my idea for an Ebon Dragon-related plot.<br /> <br /> Got a Lunar character in another game for myself. Her father (an unExalted Tepet scholar) and mother (a living pillar of flame demon) are both alive and kicking and have a truly bizarre relationship. The ST sprung that surprise on me, that was pretty fun. My fellow Lunar is currently a Cathak enlightened mortal aspiring to impress her difficult mother by Exalting (won't Exalt quite in the way mommy dearest will like <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> One of my absolute favorite characters of all time was the Half-Caste daughter of one of my Solars in the same game, who I ended up abandoning for her because she was just far more engaging. He was a bit of a rogue/wastrel, remarked on for having had a number of children in his career as a pirate, and she was a serious-minded martial artist who aspired to break out of her cultures' repressive social structures. (As for him, his parents were Dynasts who were deeply disappointed in him.)<br /> <br /> I consider intense family drama to be almost vital to characters, really.<br /> <br /> Also, consider this concept: orphan whose ghost parents follow him around and he doesn't have the heart to send them away. They're constantly trying to get him to do more with his life.<br /> <br /> Amnesiacs should be an exceptionally rare one, can't disagree. I've actually done things, though, where the character has no idea of their <i>true</i> past and have a web of lies that fall apart as they discover more about themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T18:57:15-08:00","id":1006956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/979475-seriously-is-every-friggin-solar-an-orphan?p=1006826#post1006826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, consider this concept: orphan whose ghost parents follow him around and he doesn't have the heart to send them away. They're constantly trying to get him to do more with his life.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be a spectacular second act twist to the romance of an exorcist.<br /> <br /> &quot;They refuse to move on until I've settled down.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;So you decided to date someone who banishes ghosts for a living?!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, you know, I wanted to be sure.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}